      "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{270}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ or $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{270}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={270}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{270}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{270}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{270}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
